        "heading": "How has Colorado's federal contracting trended so far in FY2026?",
        "body": "Colorado's federal contract obligations for FY2026 to date total $10.3B. Colorado's obligations are down 36.1% year over year. Colorado recorded $16.1B in FY25 and $15B in FY24, showing that FY26 to date is lower than the prior full fiscal years. The award count stands at 17,692 with an average award size of $582K."
      },
      {
        "heading": "Which agencies and industries are the largest spenders in Colorado?",
        "body": "The Department of Defense is the largest buying agency with $5.9B in obligations. The National Aeronautics and Space Administration, Department of Veterans Affairs, and Department of Energy follow with $924M, $830M, and $707M respectively. Aircraft Manufacturing, Research and Development in the Physical, Engineering, and Life Sciences (except Nanotechnology and Biotechnology), and Engineering Services lead industries with $1.5B, $1.2B, and $854M respectively. Facilities Support Services and Guided Missile and Space Vehicle Manufacturing also appear among the top industries at $662M and $695M."
      }
